{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.c1a08e3b01","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-7","passage":"<p>The university announced that ______ decision surprised many observers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["its","it's","their","they're"],"answer":"A","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the university,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.d09ef1d346","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-7","passage":"<p>The university announced that ______ annual budget would be released next week.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","it's","they're","its"],"answer":"D","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the university,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.815febeac8","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-9","passage":"<p>The zoo announced that ______ annual budget would be released next week.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","its","they're","it's"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the zoo,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.45f7632f77","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_pron","group":"pron-o-9","passage":"<p>The zoo announced that ______ latest report was available online.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","its","they're","it's"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the zoo,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.18e9c5c0b3","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_form.build_tense","group":"tense-4","passage":"<p>Since 2015, the orchestra ______ several free concerts in the park.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["had performed","performed","has performed","will perform"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “Since 2015,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has performed.”"}
